ONE IMPORTANT QUALIFICATION ON THE VERSION
------------------------------------------

Eyed's own code is GPL-3.0-**or-later**. The application *as built and
distributed* is GPL-3.0-**only**, because it links Termux's
`terminal-emulator` and `terminal-view`, which are GPL-3.0-only. No
recipient of the APK may exercise the "or later" option over that code, so
the combined work can only be conveyed under version 3. Take Eyed's code out
of the combination and the "or later" is yours again.

docs/LICENSING.md explains this in full, with the compatibility matrix.


LINEAGE
-------

Seeker IDE is a fork of **Conquest Code** (GPL-3.0-or-later), which supplies
the editor, the Debian userland, the terminal, the LSP client, git and the
ACP agent panel. Conquest Code in turn reuses **Zed**'s Rust engine crates
(GPL-3.0-or-later and Apache-2.0, Zed Industries) and vendors **Termux**'s
terminal libraries (GPL-3.0-only, Fredrik Fornwall and the Termux
contributors), which themselves derive from **Android Terminal Emulator**
(Apache-2.0, Jack Palevich). Seeker IDE adds the Solana layer on top and
rebuilds the shell for the Seeker's screen.

Every one of those notices is preserved deliberately. A fork that drops the
notices of the work it is built on is the most common GPL violation there
is, and it is not one this project intends to commit.


